\begin{align*}
\alpha^2 - \alpha - 1 &= 0 \\
\beta^2 - \beta - 1 &= 0 \\
\end{align*}
$\setlength{\unitlength}{2pt}$$
\begin{align*}
\implies (\alpha^2 - \alpha - 1)^2 - (\alpha^2 - \alpha - 1) - 1 &= 0 \\
\implies \alpha^4 - 3\alpha^3 &= -2 \\
\implies \alpha^5 - 3\alpha^4 &= -2\alpha \\
\end{align*}
which implies to
\begin{align*}
b\alpha + c = -2\alpha \\
b\beta + c = -2\beta
\end{align*}
$\end{align*}

From the first equation, $b = -2$.  From the second equation, $bc = 2\alpha+2 \alpha^2$.  Since $\alpha^2 - \alpha - 1 = 0 \implies \alpha^2 = \alpha + 1$, we find that $bc = 2(\alpha + \alpha^2) = -4$.  Therefore, $bc = \boxed{-4}$.
